Source: synctang
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tobias Mueller <muelli@cryptobitch.de>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/muelli/synctang
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: synctang-unlocker
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, cryptsetup
Description: on-demand LUKS unlocker, machine side (dracut agent)
 synctang is an on-demand LUKS volume unlocker for dracut-based boots: a
 machine asks, a human key holder on a laptop or phone answers. There is
 no always-on server; unattended reboots are out of scope by design.
 .
 This package ships "unlocker", which runs inside the dracut initrd as a
 systemd password agent, and on the booted system to enrol or revoke a
 key holder's LUKS2 keyslot and token.

Package: synctang-keyholder
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: on-demand LUKS unlocker, key holder side (laptop CLI)
 synctang is an on-demand LUKS volume unlocker for dracut-based boots: a
 machine asks, a human key holder on a laptop or phone answers. There is
 no always-on server; unattended reboots are out of scope by design.
 .
 This package ships "keyholder", the laptop-side CLI that holds a
 long-term key and answers a machine's recovery attempts on demand.

Package: synctang-dracut
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, synctang-unlocker, cryptsetup, ca-certificates
Description: on-demand LUKS unlocker, dracut module
 synctang is an on-demand LUKS volume unlocker for dracut-based boots: a
 machine asks, a human key holder on a laptop or phone answers. There is
 no always-on server; unattended reboots are out of scope by design.
 .
 This package ships the "90unlocker" dracut module, which starts the
 unlocker agent alongside the ordinary console passphrase prompt during
 early boot, and stops it before pivoting to the real root.
